 there's a real consequence he writes we  wind up with safer art and discourse  that provokes and disturbs and shocks  less it gives us culture whose artistic  value has been replaced by moral  judgment and leaves us with  mono-criticism so maybe the real answer  is that yes art should be moral but its  main moral obligation is to be truthful  about the world in which case art that  shows the world's immorality truthfully  is a bit ironically  in terms of morality but what do you  guys think are the autonomous right that  ethics has no role to play in evaluating  art are moralists like tolstoy right  that immoral art makes us hedonos is  morality and art really just truth and  if so can immoral art actually be  totally moral let us know what you think  in the comments big thanks to our  patrons for all your support and be sure  to stop by our updated patreon page and  don't forget to check us out on tick  tock clutch that subscribe button like  it's tip tipper gore string of pearls  and don't forget to ring that bell and  as always thanks for watching later  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]

